body:
_🛠️ Refactor suggestion_

**Extract duplicated helper functions to a shared test utilities module.**

The helper functions `parse_python` and `get_wrapped_module_body` are duplicated from `test_static_bundler.rs`. This violates the DRY principle.


Create a new module `test_utils.rs` and move these shared functions there:

```diff
+// tests/test_utils.rs
+use anyhow::Result;
+use ruff_python_ast::{ModModule, Stmt};
+use ruff_python_parser::parse_module;
+
+pub fn parse_python(source: &str) -> Result<ModModule> {
+    Ok(parse_module(source)?.into_syntax())
+}
+
+pub fn get_wrapped_module_body(wrapped_ast: &ModModule) -> &Vec<Stmt> {
+    assert_eq!(wrapped_ast.body.len(), 1);
+    match &wrapped_ast.body[0] {
+        Stmt::ClassDef(class_def) => &class_def.body,
+        _ => panic!("Expected a class definition"),
+    }
+}
```

Then update both test files to use the shared module:
```diff
-use anyhow::Result;
 use cribo::static_bundler::StaticBundler;
-use ruff_python_ast::{ModModule, Stmt};
-use ruff_python_parser::parse_module;
+use ruff_python_ast::Stmt;

-/// Helper function to parse Python code into an AST
-fn parse_python(source: &str) -> Result<ModModule> {
-    Ok(parse_module(source)?.into_syntax())
-}
-
-/// Helper function to get the body of a wrapped module
-fn get_wrapped_module_body(wrapped_ast: &ModModule) -> &Vec<Stmt> {
-    // The wrapped module should have exactly one statement: the wrapper class
-    assert_eq!(wrapped_ast.body.len(), 1);
-
-    // Extract the class body
-    match &wrapped_ast.body[0] {
-        Stmt::ClassDef(class_def) => &class_def.body,
-        _ => panic!("Expected a class definition"),
-    }
-}
+mod test_utils;
+use test_utils::{parse_python, get_wrapped_module_body};
```


<!-- suggestion_start -->

<details>
<summary>📝 Committable suggestion</summary>

> ‼️ **IMPORTANT**
> Carefully review the code before committing. Ensure that it accurately replaces the highlighted code, contains no missing lines, and has no issues with indentation. Thoroughly test & benchmark the code to ensure it meets the requirements.

```suggestion
// crates/cribo/tests/test_static_bundler_advanced.rs

use cribo::static_bundler::StaticBundler;
use ruff_python_ast::Stmt;

mod test_utils;
use test_utils::{parse_python, get_wrapped_module_body};

// …all of your existing test functions follow…
```

</details>

<!-- suggestion_end -->

<details>
<summary>🤖 Prompt for AI Agents</summary>

```
In crates/cribo/tests/test_static_bundler_advanced.rs around lines 7 to 21, the
helper functions parse_python and get_wrapped_module_body are duplicated from
another test file, violating the DRY principle. To fix this, create a new shared
test utilities module named test_utils.rs, move these two functions into it, and
then update this test file and test_static_bundler.rs to import and use the
functions from test_utils.rs instead of defining them locally.
```

</details>

