body:
_🛠️ Refactor suggestion_

**Avoid defaulting to a hard-coded `"1"` user – make `userId` mandatory**

Passing an implicit `userId="1"` can lead to:

1. Silent data leakage between accounts during multi-user demos.
2. Hard-to-trace bugs in e2e tests where auth is mocked.
3. Network chatter for anonymous visitors.

Prefer an explicit prop or derive it from the auth context:

```diff
-interface UserProfileProviderProps {
-  children: React.ReactNode;
-  userId?: string;
-}
+interface UserProfileProviderProps {
+  children: React.ReactNode;
+  userId: string; // required
+}

-export function UserProfileProvider({ children, userId = "1" }: UserProfileProviderProps) {
+export function UserProfileProvider({ children, userId }: UserProfileProviderProps) {
```



<!-- suggestion_start -->

<details>
<summary>📝 Committable suggestion</summary>

> ‼️ **IMPORTANT**
> Carefully review the code before committing. Ensure that it accurately replaces the highlighted code, contains no missing lines, and has no issues with indentation. Thoroughly test & benchmark the code to ensure it meets the requirements.

```suggestion
interface UserProfileProviderProps {
  children: React.ReactNode;
  userId: string; // required
}

export function UserProfileProvider({ children, userId }: UserProfileProviderProps) {
  const queryClient = useQueryClient();
  // ...rest of implementation
}
```

</details>

<!-- suggestion_end -->

<details>
<summary>🤖 Prompt for AI Agents</summary>

```
In client/src/hooks/use-user-profile.tsx around lines 68 to 73, the userId prop
is defaulted to the hard-coded string "1", which can cause data leakage and
testing issues. Remove the default value assignment for userId in the
UserProfileProvider function signature to make it mandatory. Ensure that the
caller explicitly provides a userId or derive it from the authentication context
instead of relying on a default.
```

</details>

