body:
_🛠️ Refactor suggestion_

**Consider using proper migrations instead of inline table creation.**

Creating the users table within a helper function is unconventional and could cause issues with parallel test execution. Consider using Laravel's migration system for better test isolation and maintainability.



Instead of creating tables inline, use a test migration file or leverage Laravel's built-in user migration:

```php
// In your test setup or TestCase
Schema::create('users', function (Blueprint $table) {
    $table->id();
    $table->string('name');
    $table->string('email')->unique();
    $table->string('password')->nullable();
    $table->timestamps();
});
```

Or better yet, use Laravel's default user migration and a proper User model for testing.

<details>
<summary>🤖 Prompt for AI Agents</summary>

```
In tests/Feature/StravaIntegrationTest.php around lines 190 to 216, avoid
creating the users table inline within the createTestUser function as it can
cause issues with parallel test execution and maintainability. Instead, remove
the Schema::create call from this function and use Laravel's migration system to
create the users table before tests run, either by running the default Laravel
user migration or creating a dedicated test migration. Also, use a proper User
model for testing rather than an anonymous class, ensuring the test environment
is isolated and consistent.
```

</details>

