body:
_🛠️ Refactor suggestion_

**Possible state update after unmount – guard asynchronous fetch.**

If the user navigates away before `getAvailableExercisesForStrengthGoals()` resolves, the component will try to call `setExercises`/`setIsLoadingData` on an unmounted component. Protect with an `isMounted` flag or `AbortController`.

```diff
  useEffect(() => {
-    const loadExerciseData = async () => {
+    let active = true;            // <-- guard
+    const loadExerciseData = async () => {
       try {
         setIsLoadingData(true);
         const exerciseData = await GoalProgressEngine.getAvailableExercisesForStrengthGoals();
-        setExercises(exerciseData);
+        if (active) setExercises(exerciseData);
       } catch (error) {
         console.error('Error loading exercise data:', error);
       } finally {
-        setIsLoadingData(false);
+        if (active) setIsLoadingData(false);
       }
     };
     if (user) loadExerciseData();
+
+    return () => {
+      active = false; // cleanup
+    };
   }, [user]);
```



<!-- suggestion_start -->

<details>
<summary>📝 Committable suggestion</summary>

> ‼️ **IMPORTANT**
> Carefully review the code before committing. Ensure that it accurately replaces the highlighted code, contains no missing lines, and has no issues with indentation. Thoroughly test & benchmark the code to ensure it meets the requirements.

```suggestion
  // Load exercise data for goal creation
  useEffect(() => {
    let active = true; // guard against setting state on unmounted component

    const loadExerciseData = async () => {
      try {
        setIsLoadingData(true);
        const exerciseData = await GoalProgressEngine.getAvailableExercisesForStrengthGoals();
        if (active) setExercises(exerciseData);
      } catch (error) {
        console.error('Error loading exercise data:', error);
      } finally {
        if (active) setIsLoadingData(false);
      }
    };

    if (user) {
      loadExerciseData();
    }

    return () => {
      active = false;
    };
  }, [user]);
```

</details>

<!-- suggestion_end -->

<details>
<summary>🤖 Prompt for AI Agents</summary>

```
In client/src/pages/new-goal.tsx around lines 29 to 46, the asynchronous fetch
in useEffect may update state after the component unmounts, causing potential
memory leaks or errors. Fix this by adding an isMounted flag that is set to true
at the start of the effect and false in a cleanup function. Only call
setExercises and setIsLoadingData if isMounted is still true. Alternatively, use
an AbortController to cancel the fetch on unmount and avoid state updates.
```

</details>

