![high](https://www.gstatic.com/codereviewagent/high-priority.svg)

State is being updated directly within the render body of the component (`setWasStreaming` and `setIsExpanded`). This is a violation of React's rules, can lead to unexpected behavior or infinite loops, and will cause errors in Strict Mode.

Side effects, such as updating state based on prop changes, should be handled within a `useEffect` hook. The `wasStreaming` state seems intended to track the previous value of `isStreaming`, which can be simplified by just using an effect that depends on `isStreaming`.

```typescript
useEffect(() => {
    if (!isStreaming) {
      setIsExpanded(false);
    }
  }, [isStreaming]);
```

