![medium](https://www.gstatic.com/codereviewagent/medium-priority.svg)

The error handling for a non-existent ticket relies on string matching (`error.message.includes('not found')`), which is brittle. It's better to check for the specific error type. A more robust approach is to check the error's `name` property for `'TicketNotFoundError'`. This also allows you to use the pre-formatted error message from the error object itself.

```suggestion
        if (error instanceof Error && error.message.includes('not found')) {
          console.error(`Ticket not found: ${id}`);
          process.exit(1);
        }
```

