        )) {
            $output->writeln("<info>🔄 Cloning {$selected}...</info>");

            $repoName = basename($selected, '.git');
-           exec("git clone {$selected} {$repoName}", $gitOutput, $exitCode);
+           $process = new Process(['git', 'clone', $selected, $repoName]);
+           $process->run();
+           $exitCode = $process->getExitCode();
```

</details>

<!-- suggestion_end -->

<details>
<summary>🤖 Prompt for AI Agents</summary>

```
In src/Commands/ReposCommand.php between lines 176 and 199, the selected
repository URL is directly interpolated into the shell command for cloning,
which poses a shell injection risk. To fix this, replace the direct
interpolation with either the Symfony Process component to safely run the git
clone command or wrap the $selected variable with escapeshellarg() to properly
escape it before passing to exec(). This ensures the command is executed
securely without injection vulnerabilities.
```

</details>

