![medium](https://www.gstatic.com/codereviewagent/medium-priority.svg)

It's great that you're replacing `any` with specific types. However, for `MockModal.Title`, `MockModal.Body`, and `MockModal.Footer`, you've used a duplicated inline type `{ children: ReactNode }`. This is inconsistent with the other changes in this file where you've used named types (e.g., `MockModalProps`, `MockBadgeProps`).

To improve consistency and maintainability, I recommend defining a shared type for these components' props. For example:

```typescript
interface MockModalChildProps {
    children: React.ReactNode;
}

// Then use it like this:
MockModal.Title = ({ children }: MockModalChildProps) => (
// ...
```

This will make the code cleaner and easier to maintain.

