![high](https://www.gstatic.com/codereviewagent/high-priority.svg)

The error returned by `c.getPersonBiography(p.ID)` is being ignored (assigned to `_`). If fetching the biography fails for reasons other than `sql.ErrNoRows` (which `getPersonBiography` handles by returning `nil` error), this error will be silently lost. This could mask underlying issues with the `people-biographies` database or the query itself. It's recommended to handle this error, at least by logging it.

```go
		bio, errBio := c.getPersonBiography(p.ID)
		if errBio != nil {
			// Log the error, e.g., log.Printf("Error fetching biography for person %s: %v", p.ID, errBio)
			// Decide if this error is critical enough to stop processing or if a default/empty bio is acceptable.
		}
```

