_🛠️ Refactor suggestion_

**Performance optimization may skip important updates.**

The optimization that skips updates when the robot hasn't moved significantly could cause visual desynchronization if legs move independently of the body.



Consider tracking leg segment movement independently:

```diff
     // Skip update if robot hasn't moved significantly (performance optimization)
+    // Note: This optimization may miss independent leg movements
+    static double lastUpdateTime = 0.0;
+    double currentTime = dTimeStep; // Assuming this is available
+    bool forceUpdate = (currentTime - lastUpdateTime) > 0.1; // Force update every 100ms
+    
     if (!robotTransform) return;

     static vsg::dvec3 lastBodyPos;
     const dReal* bodyPos = dBodyGetPosition(bodyId);
     vsg::dvec3 currentPos(bodyPos[0], bodyPos[1], bodyPos[2]);
-    if (vsg::length(currentPos - lastBodyPos) < 0.001) return;
+    if (!forceUpdate && vsg::length(currentPos - lastBodyPos) < 0.001) return;
     lastBodyPos = currentPos;
+    if (forceUpdate) lastUpdateTime = currentTime;
```


> Committable suggestion skipped: line range outside the PR's diff.

<details>
<summary>🤖 Prompt for AI Agents</summary>

```
In src/Robot.cpp around lines 266 to 274, the current optimization skips updates
if the robot's body position hasn't changed significantly, which can cause
visual desynchronization when legs move independently. To fix this, modify the
logic to also track and compare the positions or states of leg segments
independently, ensuring updates occur if any leg segment has moved beyond a
threshold, not just the body position.
```

</details>

