Polling the DOM every 10ms can be CPU-intensive; consider using a MutationObserver or listening for DOMContentLoaded to detect readiness.
```suggestion
    if (document.readyState === 'complete' || document.readyState === 'interactive') {
      // DOM is already ready
      callback();
    } else {
      // Wait for DOMContentLoaded event
      document.addEventListener('DOMContentLoaded', () => {
        callback();
      });
```

