Consider adding a try-catch block around `JSON.parse(savedUser)` to handle potential parsing errors. If the data in `localStorage` is malformed, `JSON.parse` will throw an error, and without handling it, the application might crash or behave unexpectedly.

```typescript
      try {
        const user = JSON.parse(savedUser);
      } catch (e) {
        console.error('Failed to parse user data from localStorage:', e);
        throw new Error('无法解析本地存储的用户信息，数据可能已损坏。');
      }
```

