body:
_🛠️ Refactor suggestion_

**Extract duplicated CSS to reduce maintenance burden**

The CSS for the notification banner is duplicated between `insertCSS` and `removeCSS` calls. This makes maintenance harder and increases the chance of inconsistencies.

Extract the CSS to a constant:

```javascript
const AI_NOTIFICATION_CSS = `
    /* Estilo injetado para destacar que a extensão está disponível */
    body::before {
        content: "💡 Começa AI disponível - clique na extensão para acessar seus prompts!";
        position: fixed;
        top: 10px;
        right: 10px;
        background: linear-gradient(135deg, #667eea 0%, #764ba2 100%);
        color: white;
        padding: 8px 12px;
        border-radius: 6px;
        font-size: 12px;
        z-index: 10000;
        animation: slideIn 0.5s ease-out;
        max-width: 250px;
        font-family: -apple-system, BlinkMacSystemFont, 'Segoe UI', sans-serif;
    }

    @keyframes slideIn {
        from { opacity: 0; transform: translateX(100%); }
        to { opacity: 1; transform: translateX(0); }
    }
`;

// Then use it in both places:
await chrome.scripting.insertCSS({
    target: { tabId: tabId },
    css: AI_NOTIFICATION_CSS
});

// And for removal:
await chrome.scripting.removeCSS({
    target: { tabId: tabId },
    css: AI_NOTIFICATION_CSS
});
```

<details>
<summary>🤖 Prompt for AI Agents</summary>

```
In background.js between lines 177 and 231, the CSS string used in both
chrome.scripting.insertCSS and chrome.scripting.removeCSS calls is duplicated,
which complicates maintenance and risks inconsistencies. To fix this, extract
the entire CSS string into a single constant variable declared outside these
calls, then reference this constant in both insertCSS and removeCSS methods to
avoid duplication and simplify future updates.
```

</details>

