body:
The '--accept-data-loss' flag automatically accepts data loss without user confirmation, which could be dangerous in environments with existing data. Consider removing this flag or adding explicit warnings about potential data loss.
```suggestion
    console.log('🗄️  Pushing database schema...');
    const userConfirmed = await getUserConfirmation(
      '⚠️ WARNING: Using --accept-data-loss may result in data loss. Do you want to proceed? (yes/no): '
    );
    if (!userConfirmed) {
      console.log('❌ Operation aborted by user.');
      process.exit(1);
    }
```

