_🛠️ Refactor suggestion_

**Consider adding error state management**

The `loadPatients` function handles errors with `console.error` but doesn't provide user feedback. Consider adding error state management to show loading errors to users.



```diff
+const [loadingError, setLoadingError] = useState<string | null>(null)
+const [isLoading, setIsLoading] = useState(true)

 const loadPatients = async () => {
   try {
+    setIsLoading(true)
+    setLoadingError(null)
     const patientData = await getPatients()
     setPatients(patientData)
   } catch (error) {
     console.error('Error loading patients:', error)
+    setLoadingError('Failed to load patients. Please refresh the page.')
+  } finally {
+    setIsLoading(false)
   }
 }
```

<!-- suggestion_start -->

<details>
<summary>📝 Committable suggestion</summary>

> ‼️ **IMPORTANT**
> Carefully review the code before committing. Ensure that it accurately replaces the highlighted code, contains no missing lines, and has no issues with indentation. Thoroughly test & benchmark the code to ensure it meets the requirements.

```suggestion
  const [loadingError, setLoadingError] = useState<string | null>(null)
  const [isLoading, setIsLoading] = useState(true)

  useEffect(() => {
    loadPatients()
  }, [])

  const loadPatients = async () => {
    try {
      setIsLoading(true)
      setLoadingError(null)
      const patientData = await getPatients()
      setPatients(patientData)
    } catch (error) {
      console.error('Error loading patients:', error)
      setLoadingError('Failed to load patients. Please refresh the page.')
    } finally {
      setIsLoading(false)
    }
  }
```

</details>

<!-- suggestion_end -->

<details>
<summary>🤖 Prompt for AI Agents</summary>

```
In app/dashboard/reports/new/page.tsx around lines 46 to 57, the loadPatients
function catches errors but only logs them to the console without updating the
UI. Add an error state variable using useState to track loading errors, update
this state inside the catch block, and conditionally render an error message in
the component to inform users when patient data fails to load.
```

</details>

