body:
Good test addition! However, the test coverage could be more comprehensive. Consider adding tests for:

1. **TELEMETRY_ACTIVE=undefined** (default case) - should also disable telemetry
2. **TELEMETRY_ACTIVE="true"** - should explicitly enable telemetry  
3. **TELEMETRY_ACTIVE with other values** (e.g., "1", "yes") - should disable telemetry

This would ensure the new opt-in logic works correctly in all scenarios:

```typescript
it("should not send data to PostHog when TELEMETRY_ACTIVE is undefined", async () => {
    const originalValue = process.env.TELEMETRY_ACTIVE;
    delete process.env.TELEMETRY_ACTIVE;

    // ... test logic similar to the existing test

    expect(posthog.capture).not.toHaveBeenCalled();
    process.env.TELEMETRY_ACTIVE = originalValue;
});

it("should send data to PostHog when TELEMETRY_ACTIVE is explicitly true", async () => {
    const originalValue = process.env.TELEMETRY_ACTIVE;
    process.env.TELEMETRY_ACTIVE = "true";

    // ... test logic

    expect(posthog.capture).toHaveBeenCalled();
    process.env.TELEMETRY_ACTIVE = originalValue;
});
```

