![high](https://www.gstatic.com/codereviewagent/high-priority.svg)

Attaching functions directly to the `window` object (e.g., `window.openGalleryModal`) pollutes the global namespace. This can lead to naming conflicts with other scripts or third-party libraries and makes the code harder to maintain. A better approach is to encapsulate all the logic within an IIFE (Immediately Invoked Function Expression) or a module. If functions must be accessible globally (e.g., for legacy `onclick` attributes), they should be exposed under a single, unique namespace object.

```suggestion
const MyPortfolio = {};
// ... all your functions ...
MyPortfolio.openGalleryModal = openGalleryModal;
window.MyPortfolio = MyPortfolio;
```

