_💡 Verification agent_

<details>
<summary>🧩 Analysis chain</summary>

**Verify mock setup completeness for EventDashboard dependencies.**

While the mock setup is comprehensive, the failing tests suggest that the EventDashboard component might require additional dependencies or different mock configurations.





Also verify if there are any console errors or warnings during component rendering:

---

🏁 Script executed:

```shell
#!/bin/bash
# Description: Check all imports and dependencies in EventDashboard component
# Expected: Ensure all dependencies are properly mocked

rg "import.*from" src/components/EventDashboard.jsx
ast-grep --pattern 'import { $$$IMPORTS } from "$MODULE"' src/components/EventDashboard.jsx
```

Length of output: 674

---

🏁 Script executed:

```shell
#!/bin/bash
# Description: Check for any error handling or logging in EventDashboard
# Expected: Understand potential runtime issues

rg -A 3 -B 3 "console\.|logger\.|error\.|catch" src/components/EventDashboard.jsx
```

Length of output: 5453

---



</details>

**Action Required: Complete mocks for all EventDashboard imports**

Based on the imports in src/components/EventDashboard.jsx, your integration test must mock the following additional dependencies and side-effects:

• **getListOfMembers** (from `../services/api.js`)  
  Add in your `beforeEach`:
  ```js
  getListOfMembers.mockResolvedValue([]);
  ```

• **getAPIQueueStats** (from `../services/api.js`)  
  ```js
  getAPIQueueStats.mockResolvedValue({ pending: 0, processing: 0, completed: 0 });
  ```

• **logger.error** (from `../services/logger.js`)  
  ```js
  jest.spyOn(logger, 'error').mockImplementation(() => {});
  ```

• **localStorage** side-effects (used for `viking_last_sync`)  
  ```js
  jest.spyOn(window.localStorage, 'getItem').mockReturnValue(null);
  jest.spyOn(window.localStorage, 'setItem').mockImplementation(() => {});
  ```

Example diff in `EventDashboard.integration.test.jsx`:

```diff
 import { getUserRoles, getToken } from '../services/auth.js';
+import { getListOfMembers, getAPIQueueStats } from '../services/api.js';
 import databaseService from '../services/database.js';
 import helpers from '../helpers';
+import logger from '../services/logger.js';

 beforeEach(() => {
   // existing mocks…
   getUserRoles.mockResolvedValue([]);
   getToken.mockReturnValue('mock-token');
   databaseService.getSections.mockResolvedValue(mockSections);
   databaseService.hasOfflineData.mockResolvedValue(false);

+  // → Add missing API mocks
+  getListOfMembers.mockResolvedValue([]);
+  getAPIQueueStats.mockResolvedValue({ pending: 0, processing: 0, completed: 0 });
+
+  // → Suppress logger errors
+  jest.spyOn(logger, 'error').mockImplementation(() => {});
+
+  // → Stub localStorage
+  jest.spyOn(window.localStorage, 'getItem').mockReturnValue(null);
+  jest.spyOn(window.localStorage, 'setItem').mockImplementation(() => {});

   // helper mocks…
   helpers.fetchSectionEvents.mockResolvedValue([]);
   /* … */
 });
```

After adding these mocks, re-run the integration tests to confirm the failures are resolved.

<details>
<summary>🤖 Prompt for AI Agents</summary>

```
In src/components/__tests__/EventDashboard.integration.test.jsx around lines 94
to 106, the integration test is missing mocks for some imported dependencies and
side-effects used in EventDashboard.jsx. Add mocks in the beforeEach block for
getListOfMembers and getAPIQueueStats from ../services/api.js with
mockResolvedValue returning empty arrays or objects as specified. Also, spy on
logger.error from ../services/logger.js with a mock implementation that does
nothing. Finally, mock localStorage's getItem to return null and setItem with an
empty mock implementation using jest.spyOn on window.localStorage. These
additions will complete the mocks and help resolve test failures.
```

</details>

