Calling `mermaid.initialize` on every render can be costly. You could move initialization outside the effect or guard it so it only runs once.
```suggestion
  const isMermaidInitialized = useRef(false);

  useEffect(() => {
    const renderMermaid = async () => {
      if (!container.current) return;

      if (!isMermaidInitialized.current) {
        mermaid.initialize({ startOnLoad: false });
        isMermaidInitialized.current = true;
      }
```

