body:
_⚠️ Potential issue_

**Fix invalid color function: hsl() with oklch variable**

--primary is oklch; hsl(var(--primary)) won’t parse. Use the variable directly.

```diff
-  button:focus-visible {
-    outline: 2px solid hsl(var(--primary));
-    outline-offset: 2px;
-  }
+  button:focus-visible {
+    outline: 2px solid var(--primary);
+    outline-offset: 2px;
+  }
```

<!-- suggestion_start -->

<details>
<summary>📝 Committable suggestion</summary>

> ‼️ **IMPORTANT**
> Carefully review the code before committing. Ensure that it accurately replaces the highlighted code, contains no missing lines, and has no issues with indentation. Thoroughly test & benchmark the code to ensure it meets the requirements.

```suggestion
  button:focus-visible {
    outline: 2px solid var(--primary);
    outline-offset: 2px;
  }
```

</details>

<!-- suggestion_end -->

<details>
<summary>🤖 Prompt for AI Agents</summary>

```
In src/App.css around lines 280 to 283, the CSS uses hsl(var(--primary)) where
--primary is defined as an oklch color, which is invalid syntax. To fix this,
remove the hsl() function and use var(--primary) directly in the outline color
property to ensure proper parsing and rendering.
```

</details>

