body:
**suggestion (testing):** Test relies on specific upgrade IDs ('pro') that may not exist in all environments.

Consider setting up a temporary config within the test to ensure the required upgrade exists, making the test environment-independent and more reliable.

```suggestion
    test('getUpgradeById works', () => {
        // Save original config
        const originalConfig = upgradeService.config;

        // Set up a temporary config with the required upgrade
        upgradeService.config = {
            upgrades: [
                { id: 'pro', name: 'Pro Upgrade', features: ['feature1', 'feature2'] }
            ],
            combos: []
        };

        const upgrade = upgradeService.getUpgradeById('pro');
        expect(upgrade).toBeDefined();
        expect(upgrade.id).toBe('pro');

        // Restore original config
        upgradeService.config = originalConfig;
    });
```

