body:
**issue (complexity):** Consider consolidating DisableFilters and PopulateFieldFilterOptions into a single RefreshFilters method to centralize and simplify filter logic.

```csharp
// 1) Consolidate DisableFilters + PopulateFieldFilterOptions into one RefreshFilters method:
private void RefreshFilters()
{
    cmbFieldFilter.Items.Clear();
    txtExplanationFilter.Text = string.Empty;

    bool hasFields = _resultData != null
                  && _resultData.Table.Columns.Contains("Field Name")
                  && _resultData.Rows.Count > 0;

    cmbFieldFilter.Enabled      = hasFields;
    txtExplanationFilter.Enabled = hasFields;

    cmbFieldFilter.Items.Add(hasFields
        ? "-- Select a Field --"
        : "-- No fields available --");

    if (hasFields)
    {
        _resultData.Table.CaseSensitive = false;               

        var fields = _resultData.Table.AsEnumerable()
            .Select(r => r.Field<string>("Field Name"))
            .Where(s => !string.IsNullOrWhiteSpace(s))
            .Distinct()
            .OrderBy(s => s)
            .ToArray();

        cmbFieldFilter.Items.AddRange(fields);
    }

    cmbFieldFilter.SelectedIndex = 0;
}

// 2) Call RefreshFilters() exactly once in Form constructor (instead of DisableFilters) 
//    and exactly once after loading dgResultdata in btnCompare_Click:

// In constructor:
public Form1()
{
    InitializeComponent();
    // ... other wiring ...
    RefreshFilters();
}

// In btnCompare_Click, replace all PopulateFieldFilterOptions() / DisableFilters() calls with:
dgResultdata.DataSource = /* your data */;
RefreshFilters();
```

– This removes duplicated PopulateFieldFilterOptions/DisableFilters calls, centralizes all enable/disable/clear logic, and preserves existing behavior.

