_🛠️ Refactor suggestion_

**Add input validation and consider error handling.**

The handler should validate the incoming command and handle potential repository failures.



```diff
 public async Task<WorkflowEntity> Handle(CreateWorkflowCommand request, CancellationToken cancellationToken)
 {
+    // Validate input
+    if (string.IsNullOrWhiteSpace(request.Name))
+        throw new ArgumentException("Workflow name cannot be empty", nameof(request.Name));
+    
+    if (request.PriceCredits < 0)
+        throw new ArgumentException("Price credits cannot be negative", nameof(request.PriceCredits));
+
     var workflow = new WorkflowEntity
     {
         Id = Guid.NewGuid(),
         Name = request.Name,
         Description = request.Description,
         PriceCredits = request.PriceCredits,
         CreatedAt = DateTime.UtcNow,
         UpdatedAt = DateTime.UtcNow
     };

     await _repository.CreateAsync(workflow, cancellationToken);
     return workflow;
 }
```

