_🛠️ Refactor suggestion_

**Basic increment test is correct but could be more comprehensive.**

The test verifies the happy path for `incrementLoginCount`, but consider testing multiple increments and edge cases.




Add these additional test cases to improve coverage:

```typescript
it('increments login count multiple times', () => {
  const { incrementLoginCount, getState } = useSettingStore;
  incrementLoginCount();
  incrementLoginCount();
  incrementLoginCount();
  expect(getState().loginCount).toBe(3);
});

it('increments from non-zero starting count', () => {
  useSettingStore.setState({ loginCount: 5 });
  useSettingStore.getState().incrementLoginCount();
  expect(useSettingStore.getState().loginCount).toBe(6);
});
```

<details>
<summary>🤖 Prompt for AI Agents</summary>

```
In app/tests/src/stores/settingStore.test.ts around lines 13 to 16, the current
test only checks a single increment of loginCount. To improve test coverage, add
two more test cases: one that calls incrementLoginCount multiple times and
verifies the count increases accordingly, and another that sets a non-zero
initial loginCount, increments once, and verifies the count increments from that
starting value.
```

</details>

