![high](https://www.gstatic.com/codereviewagent/high-priority.svg)

The API call to fetch horses is not wrapped in a `try...catch` block. If the request fails, the error will be unhandled, and the user will see an empty table without any indication of what went wrong.

```
async function fetchHorses() {
  try {
    const res = await api.get('/horses');
    setHorses(res.data);
  } catch (error) {
    console.error('Failed to fetch horses:', error);
    // Consider setting an error state to show a message to the user.
  }
}
```

