To make this test more robust, also test the temporary disabling of game activity during the animation.

First, add `jest.useFakeTimers();` at the top of this file to enable control over `setTimeout`.

Then, update this test to assert that `gameState.gameActive` is correctly toggled:

```javascript
test('rewind animates tiles back to previous state and manages gameActive', () => {
  // initial tile
  gameState.board[0][0] = { id: 1, value: 2 };
  saveGameState();

  // simulate moved tile
  gameState.board[0][0] = { id: null, value: 0 };
  gameState.board[0][3] = { id: 1, value: 2 };
  renderBoard();

  rewindTime();
  const boardEl = document.getElementById('gameBoard');
  const firstTile = boardEl.children[0];

  expect(gameState.gameActive).toBe(false);
  expect(gameState.board[0][0].id).toBe(1);
  expect(gameState.crystals).toBe(1);
  expect(firstTile.classList.contains('move')).toBe(true);
  expect(firstTile.style.getPropertyValue('--dx')).toBe('3');

  jest.runAllTimers();
  expect(gameState.gameActive).toBe(true);
});
```

