![medium](https://img.shields.io/badge/priority-medium-yellow)

The errors from `json.Unmarshal`, `client.SendTask`, and `json.Marshal` are returned without additional context. Consider wrapping these errors to provide more specific information about where the error occurred. For instance:

```go
// For json.Unmarshal
if err := json.Unmarshal([]byte(raw), &p); err != nil {
    return "", fmt.Errorf("failed to unmarshal delegate parameters: %w", err)
}

// For client.SendTask
if err != nil {
    return "", fmt.Errorf("failed to send task via a2a client: %w", err)
}

// For json.Marshal
if err != nil {
    return "", fmt.Errorf("failed to marshal task response: %w", err)
}
```
This practice significantly aids in debugging by pinpointing the source and nature of errors.

