![medium](https://www.gstatic.com/codereviewagent/medium-priority.svg)

This is a great fix that correctly types the `inset` prop and removes the `any` type from the props object.

For improved readability and maintainability, you could consider extracting the component's props into a separate type alias. This is a common pattern that makes the component signature cleaner and is more scalable if more custom props are added in the future.

For example:

```typescript
type DropdownMenuItemProps = React.ComponentPropsWithoutRef<
  typeof DropdownMenuPrimitive.Item
> & {
  inset?: boolean;
};

const DropdownMenuItem = React.forwardRef<
  React.ElementRef<typeof DropdownMenuPrimitive.Item>,
  DropdownMenuItemProps
>(({ className, inset, ...props }, ref) => (
  // ...
));
```

While the current implementation is correct, this pattern can be beneficial as the component evolves.

