body:
_🧹 Nitpick (assertive)_

**Consider simplifying the documentation example.**

The current example shows a complete trait implementation when focusing on the `handle_error` method usage would be clearer.

Consider this more focused example:

```diff
-    /// ```no_run
-    /// # use wireframe::{ConnectionContext, WireframeProtocol, push::PushHandle};
-    /// # struct Proto;
-    /// # impl WireframeProtocol for Proto {
-    /// #     type Frame = (); type ProtocolError = &'static str;
-    /// #     fn handle_error(&self, error: Self::ProtocolError, _ctx: &mut ConnectionContext) {
-    /// #         eprintln!("error: {error}");
-    /// #     }
-    /// #     fn on_connection_setup(&self, _h: PushHandle<Self::Frame>, _c: &mut ConnectionContext) {}
-    /// #     fn before_send(&self, _f: &mut Self::Frame, _c: &mut ConnectionContext) {}
-    /// #     fn on_command_end(&self, _c: &mut ConnectionContext) {}
-    /// # }
-    /// ```
+    /// ```
+    /// # use wireframe::{ConnectionContext, WireframeProtocol};
+    /// # struct MyProtocol;
+    /// # impl WireframeProtocol for MyProtocol {
+    /// #     type Frame = Vec<u8>;
+    /// #     type ProtocolError = String;
+    /// fn handle_error(&self, error: Self::ProtocolError, ctx: &mut ConnectionContext) {
+    ///     eprintln!("Protocol error occurred: {}", error);
+    ///     // Custom error handling logic here
+    /// }
+    /// # }
+    /// ```
```

<details>
<summary>🤖 Prompt for AI Agents</summary>

```
In src/hooks.rs around lines 39 to 52, the documentation example for the
handle_error method is overly complex by showing a full trait implementation.
Simplify it by providing a focused example that only demonstrates the
handle_error method usage with minimal surrounding code. Replace the existing
example with a concise snippet that includes just the necessary imports, a
struct definition, and an implementation of handle_error with a clear error
handling print statement and a comment for custom logic.
```

</details>

