![high](https://www.gstatic.com/codereviewagent/high-priority.svg)

The logic for queuing `ArticleExtractionOperation`s (lines 825-831) is identical to the implementation in `LocalAccountDelegate.swift` (lines 227-233).

This duplication could make future modifications error-prone and harder to maintain. Would it be possible to refactor this shared logic into a common helper method or perhaps an extension on a shared protocol that both delegates conform to? This would ensure consistency and simplify updates.

```swift
// Consider refactoring this shared logic into a common helper method
let articles = articleChanges.newArticles.union(articleChanges.updatedArticles)
for article in articles {
    guard article.webFeed?.isArticleExtractorAlwaysOn ?? true else { continue }
    if let operation = ArticleExtractionOperation(article: article) {
        articleExtractionQueue.addOperation(operation)
    }
}
```

